WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.658
This practice example stores a small patient record
using separate variables The

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:10.224
values can include text numbers and a Boolean flag
depending on what we want to

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:16.183
represent Run the code and identify the type and
meaning of each variable

00:00:17.106 --> 00:00:22.619
Then change the values while keeping the variable
names clear You can also add another

00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:28.274
variable such as a condition or a blood pressure
label The important

00:00:28.301 --> 00:00:35.185
idea is that healthcare data like business data
contains different kinds of information Identifiers

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:40.316
measurements categories and status flags should be
represented in ways that match their meaning
